=20
> > * In natlang syntax, all phrases have lexical heads; so a natlang
> > grammar of Lojban would make every phrase an X Phrase, where X is
> > a selmaho.
>=20
> Huh?

Natlang syntax conforms to the principle that every phrase is a projection
of a word it dominates (=3D contains) -- this word is the head.=20
(=3D 'Endocentricity'.) A phrase that is a projection of a noun -- i.e. a
phrase headed by a noun -- is a Noun Phrase.=20

There is no such requirement in the formalism used for the formal Lojban=20
grammar, which is formally much less restrictive than endocentric grammars.

